WEBVTT

00:02.600 --> 00:09.610
Episode 15: Kyoto Sister School Exchange Event - Group Battle 1 -

00:06.520 --> 00:09.610
We're starting in one minute.

00:09.840 --> 00:16.910
Now, let's hear a few words of well-appreciated
encouragement from Iori Utahime-sensei.

00:16.910 --> 00:17.740
Huh?!

00:17.740 --> 00:20.620
U-Uh...

00:20.620 --> 00:25.460
Um, some degree of injury will be unavoidable,

00:25.460 --> 00:31.130
but, um... now and then, help
each other out... or something...

00:31.320 --> 00:32.630
Time's up.

00:32.630 --> 00:35.630
Hey! Gojou, you little...

00:35.630 --> 00:39.300
Now, let the sister school exchange event...

00:39.300 --> 00:42.600
begin!

00:42.600 --> 00:44.560
Respect your seniors!

00:45.270 --> 00:46.230
Ichiro?!

00:46.230 --> 00:47.900
So stupid.

00:48.310 --> 00:49.980
Where's Toudou?

00:49.980 --> 00:52.940
What makes you think I would know?

00:52.940 --> 00:54.530
Can't we all get along?

01:03.830 --> 01:06.500
Where do you think
the cursed spirit boss is?

01:06.500 --> 01:09.590
It was probably unleashed
halfway between both schools,

01:09.590 --> 01:11.960
but it's not just going to sit still.

01:12.340 --> 01:13.880
At the time we agreed upon,

01:13.880 --> 01:17.590
we'll split up into the Megumi squad
and the Panda squad for scouting.

01:17.590 --> 01:19.970
We'll be counting on you after that, Yuuji.

01:19.970 --> 01:20.800
Yeah!

01:25.390 --> 01:28.900
Where are you going?

01:30.190 --> 01:31.520
That's small fry.

01:36.030 --> 01:37.700
Senpai, stop!

01:45.540 --> 01:48.120
Great! You're all here!

01:48.710 --> 01:51.380
Come at me all together!

01:56.090 --> 01:57.260
Scatter!

02:00.760 --> 02:02.600
Toudou was alone.

02:03.060 --> 02:05.890
We were right to swap Yuuji into that role.

02:09.850 --> 02:12.520
I already knew it, but he's a monster.

02:12.520 --> 02:13.400
Yup.

02:13.400 --> 02:15.150
So just ignore him.

02:15.150 --> 02:16.400
Tuna.

03:47.080 --> 03:50.830
JUJUTSU KAISEN

03:57.540 --> 04:04.050
Before the Exchange Event Started

03:59.920 --> 04:04.050
Toudou will absolutely be
out to crush us straight away.

04:04.390 --> 04:08.310
Mai might follow behind him
to come after me, too.

04:09.220 --> 04:11.230
Toudou's a monster.

04:11.770 --> 04:16.150
The worst possible outcome would be
that we all face him and get wiped out.

04:18.440 --> 04:21.570
So our plan was to leave just one person,

04:21.570 --> 04:24.530
either Panda or Megumi,
behind to occupy him, but...

04:25.910 --> 04:28.450
Itadori, we'll leave that role to you.

04:30.200 --> 04:33.290
We'd rather not lose anyone
who can scout out our enemies.

04:34.040 --> 04:35.540
You don't have to beat him.

04:35.540 --> 04:38.380
Just hold out as long as
possible and buy us time.

04:38.380 --> 04:40.420
But you can be daring against him!

04:40.420 --> 04:43.300
To be blunt, we weren't counting
on your abilities anyway,

04:43.300 --> 04:45.470
so it won't affect us too
much if you have to quit.

04:45.470 --> 04:46.720
That's mean!

04:47.300 --> 04:49.180
Sorry, Megumi.

04:49.180 --> 04:51.600
You wanted to face Toudou, didn't you?

04:52.350 --> 04:54.390
No, I'm good either way.

04:54.390 --> 04:55.980
You're super dry.

04:57.770 --> 05:00.440
But Senpai, if I'm gonna do this,

05:02.480 --> 05:04.490
then I'm gonna win.

05:08.280 --> 05:10.200
Nice speed.

05:10.740 --> 05:12.080
Seriously?

05:12.080 --> 05:14.160
I thought I landed a good one.

05:20.340 --> 05:22.170
I'll return the favor, first-year.

05:22.170 --> 05:23.960
Guard like your life depends on it!

05:26.090 --> 05:28.760
Where?

05:41.520 --> 05:43.570
My arm's... still here?

05:44.530 --> 05:46.740
I thought it got blown off.

05:46.740 --> 05:48.820
If that cursed spirit
hadn't gotten in the way,

05:48.820 --> 05:50.490
that would have been real bad.

06:23.440 --> 06:24.610
Done already?

06:32.240 --> 06:34.910
Now, which should I pursue?

06:40.830 --> 06:42.670
Are you for real?

06:50.260 --> 06:53.890
You think you can just pound
away at my head like that?!

06:53.890 --> 06:56.720
What if you made me even
dumber than I already am?!

06:57.680 --> 06:59.520
Don't worry.

06:59.520 --> 07:04.440
Takada-chan said, "Men are perfect
when they're a little dumb."

07:04.610 --> 07:06.150
Who's that?

07:06.150 --> 07:08.400
I'm not interested in any idols.

07:08.400 --> 07:11.160
Then how did you know she's an idol?

07:11.160 --> 07:13.070
You know who she is, don't you?

07:13.700 --> 07:16.200
What's your name, first-year?

07:16.200 --> 07:17.700
Itadori Yuuji.

07:17.700 --> 07:20.290
I see. Itadori Yuuji.

07:20.290 --> 07:22.710
I have one question for you.

07:24.460 --> 07:26.710
What kind of woman is your type?

07:27.670 --> 07:28.460
Huh?

07:29.470 --> 07:31.380
What's my type?

07:31.380 --> 07:33.390
Why are you asking me that right now?

07:33.720 --> 07:37.220
Don't worry about that.
I'm just appraising you.

07:39.560 --> 07:43.730
I don't really get it, but if I had to say...

07:47.360 --> 07:51.820
A tall woman with a big ass, I guess?

07:52.150 --> 07:54.070
Like Jennifer Lawrence.

08:09.300 --> 08:12.170
The new series is pretty good.

08:12.170 --> 08:12.900
Oh?

08:29.570 --> 08:31.610
I'm going to confess to Takada-chan.

08:32.030 --> 08:33.900
Huh?! Don't do that!

08:33.900 --> 08:35.990
I don't wanna have to comfort you later!

08:35.990 --> 08:37.490
That's such a pain!

08:37.490 --> 08:40.040
Why are you assuming she'll reject me?

08:42.500 --> 08:46.040
I could ask you why you
think she'll say yes.

08:46.040 --> 08:50.090
Anne Sullivan once said to Helen Keller,

08:50.090 --> 08:54.260
"What fool thinks of defeat
before even trying?"

08:54.260 --> 08:56.050
Inoki was the one who said that.

08:57.430 --> 08:59.300
I'm sorry.

08:59.300 --> 09:01.560
I'm already in love with someone.

09:19.370 --> 09:22.080
Any chance that someone is me?

09:22.620 --> 09:24.500
No way, man.

09:27.540 --> 09:29.040
Come on, let's go.

09:31.840 --> 09:33.960
I'll treat you to some ramen.

09:49.980 --> 09:53.230
You never lost to anyone
in your hometown, huh?

09:55.610 --> 09:59.870
Seems like we're best friends!

09:59.870 --> 10:01.910
When you just learned my name?!

10:03.490 --> 10:05.750
Yeah, continue straight that way.

10:05.750 --> 10:07.330
Toudou-kun's there, though.

10:07.600 --> 10:08.960
Not a problem.

10:08.960 --> 10:11.290
He's the one who told us to do as we pleased.

10:19.260 --> 10:22.010
New Shadow Style, Simple Domain:

10:24.390 --> 10:25.560
Quick Draw!

10:30.850 --> 10:32.770
What reflexes!

10:32.770 --> 10:36.570
I know I hesitated, but still,
my counter didn't even scratch him!

10:42.240 --> 10:43.870
I'm surrounded?

10:44.540 --> 10:45.340
Wait...

10:46.700 --> 10:49.370
Are these guys...

10:52.960 --> 10:54.840
trying to kill me?

11:00.430 --> 11:01.390
This is...

11:02.800 --> 11:05.260
Itadori and I switched places?!

11:06.890 --> 11:07.930
Hey.

11:09.440 --> 11:13.520
I told you I'd kill you if
you interfered, didn't I?

11:14.150 --> 11:15.570
No, you didn't.

11:15.570 --> 11:18.530
You said you'd kill us if
we ordered you around.

11:18.900 --> 11:20.570
Was that Itadori's...

11:20.570 --> 11:23.280
No, it was Toudou's technique?

11:23.530 --> 11:26.330
Same thing. Piss off!

11:33.750 --> 11:35.170
Looks like he's retreating.

11:35.170 --> 11:36.590
Lame.

11:36.590 --> 11:38.080
Thank goodness!

11:38.880 --> 11:40.590
Make sure you kill him.

11:41.300 --> 11:43.590
That depends on Itadori.

11:43.590 --> 11:45.470
Don't order me around.

11:45.780 --> 11:47.260
What's with these people,

11:47.260 --> 11:49.980
trying to kill me and then
arguing with each other?

11:51.350 --> 11:57.110
After all, I'm not an inconsiderate man
who'd hold back against his best friend!

12:04.950 --> 12:08.080
This is why I said to leave him be.

12:08.080 --> 12:10.290
We're off to a rocky start.

12:10.700 --> 12:15.210
We can't start hunting down cursed spirits
without me scouting from the air, either.

12:17.380 --> 12:19.760
They're all such a hassle.

12:20.210 --> 12:21.720
Hang in there, me.

12:21.720 --> 12:23.130
You're as cute as ever today.

12:23.340 --> 12:24.430
Take her down.

12:26.560 --> 12:27.260
Oh, no.

12:29.260 --> 12:32.560
Mai, Mechamaru, cover Nishimiya.

12:32.560 --> 12:33.390
At once.

12:33.390 --> 12:36.280
Well, we are in trouble without her.

12:47.950 --> 12:50.950
Kamo-san, are you guys

12:51.540 --> 12:53.580
planning to kill Itadori?

13:00.170 --> 13:02.970
JUJUTSU KAISEN

13:05.630 --> 13:07.970
JUJUTSU KAISEN

13:11.790 --> 13:12.620
That's strange.

13:12.620 --> 13:13.600
It is strange.

13:14.390 --> 13:16.900
All the Kyoto students are moving together.

13:17.600 --> 13:20.110
Toward the area we left Yuuji in.

13:20.110 --> 13:22.690
I think that puts everyone from Kyoto there?

13:23.490 --> 13:26.320
You mean that's where the target is?

13:26.320 --> 13:29.910
No, unless the second-grade
is especially cunning,

13:29.910 --> 13:31.450
my Demon Dog would have noticed it.

13:33.290 --> 13:37.000
They're trying to kill Itadori, aren't they?

13:37.570 --> 13:39.880
What the hell?! I don't see why!

13:44.210 --> 13:45.590
It's possible.

13:46.260 --> 13:47.380
Kelp.

13:47.840 --> 13:51.390
I didn't sense that much hostility from them,

13:51.760 --> 13:54.810
but that was prior to Yuuji's surprise survival.

13:57.350 --> 14:01.420
It's entirely possible that
Principal Gakuganji would order that.

14:01.420 --> 14:07.400
Are the Kyoto students a bunch of cowards
who'd kill a person on someone else's orders?

14:07.600 --> 14:09.780
They don't see him the same way.

14:09.780 --> 14:13.410
You two have spent day after day with Yuuji.

14:13.410 --> 14:17.210
We only recently learned that
he's a good person ourselves.

14:17.210 --> 14:20.040
He's a naturally happy sort you
don't often see among sorcerers.

14:20.040 --> 14:21.420
But the thing is...

14:22.040 --> 14:24.920
To those who don't know
anything about Yuuji,

14:24.920 --> 14:29.430
the vessel of Sukuna
is just an object of fear.

14:30.010 --> 14:33.430
It wouldn't feel any different
from exorcising a curse to them.

14:34.390 --> 14:39.440
Even normal jujutsu sorcerers
can easily blur that line.

14:42.770 --> 14:44.690
We're turning back, Megumi.

14:45.400 --> 14:46.780
Sorry.

14:46.780 --> 14:48.860
What are you apologizing for, dummy?

14:49.700 --> 14:53.700
There's no point in winning or losing
the exchange event if your friend dies.

14:55.290 --> 14:59.620
Nobara and I will go back
to confirm that Yuuji's safe.

15:00.040 --> 15:01.830
He's not answering his phone, either.

15:02.170 --> 15:05.340
Toge, you keep hunting down
the cursed spirit, please.

15:05.880 --> 15:07.170
Bonito flakes.

15:07.170 --> 15:09.970
I know you're worried about Yuuji, too.

15:10.380 --> 15:13.100
But if my prediction is correct,

15:13.100 --> 15:15.600
the Kyoto students are trying

15:15.600 --> 15:19.480
to use the chaos of the group
battle to assassinate Yuuji.

15:19.880 --> 15:23.130
Once the group battle's over,
there won't be any assassination.

15:23.130 --> 15:24.320
Makes sense.

15:24.320 --> 15:25.480
Salmon.

15:25.770 --> 15:27.570
I'm worried about Maki, too.

15:27.570 --> 15:29.320
We won't let them kill Yuuji,

15:29.320 --> 15:31.110
and we'll win this group battle.

15:31.570 --> 15:32.910
Of course.

15:37.400 --> 15:40.120
Answer on the first ring, Fushiguro!

15:40.850 --> 15:45.840
Also, why didn't they provide us with
wireless radios or Bluetooth earbuds?!

15:46.760 --> 15:48.130
I wouldn't want them.

15:48.130 --> 15:51.010
They're distracting, and they startle
you when you get a call.

15:51.010 --> 15:53.470
You can take them off during combat!

15:58.680 --> 16:00.140
Ow...

16:01.940 --> 16:04.520
So that's Fushiguro-kun's Nue, huh?

16:05.020 --> 16:06.900
Electrified wings.

16:06.900 --> 16:09.570
Looks like they'll affect
my movement for a while.

16:12.110 --> 16:17.080
Nishimiya-chan!

16:17.580 --> 16:20.580
Come and play!

16:20.790 --> 16:22.460
So crass!

16:22.460 --> 16:23.830
Not cute at all.

16:24.420 --> 16:28.300
Kamo-san, are you guys
planning to kill Itadori?

16:28.710 --> 16:32.300
And if I said we were?

16:32.500 --> 16:34.280
You failed, then.

16:34.640 --> 16:37.810
Itadori wouldn't go down in such a short time.

16:42.140 --> 16:43.730
We have no reason to kill him.

16:44.310 --> 16:45.900
Yes, you do.

16:45.900 --> 16:48.520
The higher-ups and the three
major clans have plenty.

17:20.970 --> 17:22.520
What splendid toughness!

17:22.520 --> 17:25.560
He's actively using the landscape
to his advantage, too!

17:27.290 --> 17:28.110
He's gone?

17:31.730 --> 17:33.650
He's also quick to set up his next move!

17:41.440 --> 17:43.670
And to top it off...

17:46.050 --> 17:48.130
He has such tremendous power!

17:48.460 --> 17:51.590
His raw strength is greater than mine,
despite his small body!

17:51.590 --> 17:54.630
Which is why his blows are effective
with so little cursed energy!

17:55.300 --> 17:59.640
And that makes it hard to read his movements
from the flow of cursed energy!

17:59.890 --> 18:03.220
But the way this cursed
energy hits after a time lag...

18:03.220 --> 18:06.060
That's just... That's just...

18:07.390 --> 18:10.860
...wrong!

18:10.860 --> 18:14.070
...wrong!

18:12.520 --> 18:15.650
...wrong!

18:14.150 --> 18:17.320
...wrong!

18:15.860 --> 18:18.990
...wrong!

18:17.570 --> 18:20.700
...wrong!

18:23.370 --> 18:25.160
Was that Toudou?

18:25.660 --> 18:27.160
It was.

18:27.160 --> 18:32.340
I think I understand why you
failed to finish off Yuuji.

18:33.210 --> 18:36.720
So why did you distance
yourself from Noritoshi?

18:36.720 --> 18:39.760
Are you keeping your technique
a secret from your allies, too?

18:44.390 --> 18:47.390
I'm sorry about Itadori-kun.

18:47.390 --> 18:51.270
I know this is an excuse,
but I'm not like the others.

18:51.610 --> 18:56.400
Still, that doesn't mean I plan to hand
over victory in this exchange event.

18:56.780 --> 19:01.780
Recommendation

18:57.780 --> 19:01.780
You know that sorcerers advance in rank
through a recommendation system, right?

19:02.240 --> 19:07.120
The exchange event is often discussed among
sorcerers without connections up the chain.

19:07.910 --> 19:09.920
Students who perform well here

19:09.920 --> 19:13.790
are granted many chances to
advance while they're studying.

19:14.920 --> 19:19.050
Coincidentally, the person in charge
of a student can't recommend them.

19:15.170 --> 19:24.300
Recommendation

19:19.470 --> 19:24.300
For example, Gojou-san couldn't
recommend Itadori-kun to be a first-grade.

19:24.850 --> 19:29.310
I want to become independent as
quickly as possible so I can earn money.

19:33.810 --> 19:34.770
Why?

19:37.900 --> 19:39.190
I'm poor!

19:39.190 --> 19:40.820
And I have two little brothers!

19:40.900 --> 19:42.700
Are you okay?

19:43.120 --> 19:44.910
Are you getting along well enough with Mai?

19:44.910 --> 19:46.540
Aren't you too nice a person?

19:46.540 --> 19:49.290
Huh? Probably...

19:50.640 --> 19:52.670
I won't hold back, you know.

19:53.960 --> 19:55.460
Not a problem!

19:55.460 --> 19:58.170
That's not what I said all that for, anyway!

20:00.630 --> 20:02.010
My friend!

20:02.010 --> 20:04.510
That cursed energy you
blast with a time lag...

20:04.510 --> 20:06.890
That's a bad habit of yours!

20:06.890 --> 20:08.680
You mean Divergent Fist?

20:09.680 --> 20:11.850
What's he on about all of a sudden?

20:13.400 --> 20:17.440
So long as you're satisfied with that,
you'll never beat me!

20:18.320 --> 20:20.900
If you're satisfied with
staying on that level,

20:20.900 --> 20:24.070
you and I won't stay best friends.

20:24.780 --> 20:26.330
Are you okay with that?!

20:26.330 --> 20:29.450
I don't know. I don't care about that.

20:29.450 --> 20:31.790
Are you okay with staying weak?

20:35.880 --> 20:37.500
No, I'm not!

20:39.250 --> 20:40.880
That's right!

20:41.590 --> 20:44.550
My best friend!

22:14.980 --> 22:17.480
Juju Stroll

22:17.480 --> 22:21.730
Q: What kind of person is your type?

22:22.440 --> 22:25.990
Someone who's stronger
than me, at the very least.

22:26.400 --> 22:30.240
Huh? What makes you think I'll answer?

22:30.690 --> 22:33.750
I totally can't stand a UBSSD.

22:32.890 --> 22:34.900
Useless

22:33.260 --> 22:34.900
Broke

22:33.640 --> 22:34.900
Smelly

22:34.020 --> 22:34.900
Stingy

22:34.390 --> 22:34.900
Dead

22:35.240 --> 22:37.780
Do you know who Sebastian Stan is?

22:39.290 --> 22:41.170
He has a great body.

22:41.530 --> 22:47.570
Well, you know, I like
hot guys, like most girls,

22:47.570 --> 22:50.840
but I want someone fun to be around, too,

22:50.840 --> 22:57.560
and it's important whether or not he can
make you feel like he's the only one for you.

23:00.050 --> 23:02.720
Oh, gosh, how embarrassing!

23:03.380 --> 23:07.020
Uh, you know, uh, um...

23:07.020 --> 23:08.860
Wh-What was it?

23:09.510 --> 23:10.690
Um...

23:10.690 --> 23:11.860
Um, um, um...

23:11.860 --> 23:13.380
You know, that girl who seemed nice.

23:13.380 --> 23:14.540
The one who seemed nice.

23:14.540 --> 23:16.340
With the notable bangs.

23:16.340 --> 23:18.580
Come on, come on, you know! That one girl!

23:20.050 --> 23:23.470
Nice girl, nice girl, nice girl...

23:40.330 --> 23:42.240
Oh, Miwa?

23:42.240 --> 23:43.700
Yeah! Her, her, her, her, her!

23:51.550 --> 23:56.340
Episode 16:
Kyoto Sister School Exchange Event - Group Battle 2 -
